          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#quantization_of_greenschwarz_super_brane_sigma_models
            Quantization of Green-Schwarz super
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            Light cone gauge quantization is the only method by which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super+p-brane+sigma+models"} Green-Schwarz super p-brane sigma models
            have been quantized, to date.
          %h3#bfss_matrix_model BFSS matrix model
          %p
            Specifically, applying light-cone gauge quantization to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            on 11d
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            yields the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
          %h3#bmn_matrix_model BMN matrix model
          %p
            Alternatively, applying the light cone gauge quantization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            not on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            but, more generally, on 11d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pp-wave+spacetimes"} pp-wave spacetimes
            (which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+limits"} Penrose limits
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
