                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans-Christian+Pauli"}> Hans-Christian Pauli
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+J.+Brodsky"} Stanley J. Brodsky
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Discretized light-cone quantization: Solution to a field theory in one space and one time dimension
                %strong 32
                (1985) 2001 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.32.2001"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.32.2001
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#BrodskyPauliPinsky98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Brodsky"}> Stanley Brodsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans-Christian+Pauli"} Hans-Christian Pauli
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+S.+Pinsky"} Stephen S. Pinsky
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Chromodynamics and Other Field Theories on the Light Cone
                %strong 301
                (1998) 299-486 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9705477"}> arXiv:hep-ph/9705477
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-1573(97)00089-6"} doi:10.1016/S0370-1573(97)00089-6
          %p
            Review in the broader context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yitzhak+Frishman"}> Yitzhak Frishman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Sonnenschein"} Jacob Sonnenschein
              = succeed "," do
                %em Non-Perturbative Field Theory – From Two Dimensional Conformal Field Theory to QCD in Four Dimensions
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511770838"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511770838
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.4859"} arXiv:1004.4859
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009401654"} doi:10.1017/9781009401654
          %p
            A light-cone QCD-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            adapted to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MHV+amplitudes"} MHV amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              Hiren Kakkad, Piotr Kotko, Anna Stasto,
              %em Quantum correction to a new Wilson line-based action for Gluodynamics
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.04101"}> arXiv:2311.04101
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              James P. Vary, Chandan Mondal, Siqi Xu, Xingbo Zhao, Yang Li:
              %em Nucleon Structure from Basis Light-Front Quantization : Status and Prospects
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.08283"}> arXiv:2512.08283
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#application_in_string_theory Application in string theory
          %p
            Light cone quantization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            originates with
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Goddard"}> Peter Goddard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Goldstone"} Jeffrey Goldstone
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Rebbi"} Claudio Rebbi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+B.+Thorn"} Charles B. Thorn
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum dynamics of a massless relativistic string
              %strong 56
              1 (1973) 109-135 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(73)90223-X"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(73)90223-X
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+B.+Thorn"}> Charles B. Thorn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Newtonian Dynamics on a Light Front
              %strong 59
              (1999) 025005 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9807151"}> arXiv:hep-th/9807151
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.59.025005"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.59.025005
          %p
            All the standard introductory texts on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            have sections devoted to light-cone quantization. For instance:
          %ul
            %li#GreenSchwarzWitten88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superstring theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/250488"} spire:250488
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/us/academic/subjects/physics/theoretical-physics-and-mathematical-physics/superstring-theory-25th-anniversary-edition-volume-1?format=HB&isbn=9781107029118"} ISBN:9781107029118
          %p
            In the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            as a discrete light-cone formulation of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %ul
            %li#Seiberg97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"}> Nathan Seiberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Why is the Matrix Model Correct?
                %strong 79
                (1997) 3577-3580 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9710009"}> arXiv:hep-th/9710009
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.79.3577"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.79.3577
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adel+Bilal"}> Adel Bilal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em DLCQ of M-Theory as the Light-Like Limit
                %strong 435
                (1998) 312-318 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805070"}> arXiv:hep-th/9805070
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-2693(98)00811-9"} doi:10.1016/S0370-2693(98)00811-9
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Ydri18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Badis+Ydri"}> Badis Ydri
              , Section 3.9 of:
              %em Review of M(atrix)-Theory, Type IIB Matrix Model and Matrix String Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.00734"}> arXiv:1708.00734
              \&amp;rbrack;, published as:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Matrix Models of String Theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/book/978-0-7503-1726-9"} ISBN:978-0-7503-1726-9
          %div
            %h3#LightConeQuantizationOfM2BranesToBFSSMatrixModel Quantization of the M2-brane sigma-model to a matrix model
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-formulation" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge"} light-cone gauge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
              for the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+membrane"} relativistic membrane
              and the corresponding matrix
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
              regularization is due to:
            %ul
              %li#Hoppe82
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum theory of a massless relativistic surface and a two-dimensional bound state problem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1721.1/15717"} dspace:1721.1/15717
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HoppeMembrane82.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p Some exact solutions:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em Exact algebraic M(em)brane solutions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.00569"} arXiv:2107.00569
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em The fast non-commutative sharp drop
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.13146"} arXiv:2302.13146
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              On the regularized
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge+quantization"} light-cone gauge quantization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              on (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"}> super
              )
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            %p Original articles:
            %ul
              %li#deWitHoppeNicolai88
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+de+Wit"}> Bernard de Wit
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"} Jens Hoppe
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Quantum Mechanics of Supermembranes
                %strong 305
                (1988) 545-581 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(88)90116-2"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(88)90116-2
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/261702"} spire:261702
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pubman.mpdl.mpg.de/pubman/item/escidoc:153408:1/component/escidoc:153407/353961.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/deWitHoppeNicolai88.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p Observation that the spectrum is continuous:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+de+Wit"}> Bernard de Wit
                , W. Lüscher,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The supermembrane is unstable
                %strong 320
                (1989) 135 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(89)90214-9"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(89)90214-9
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/266584/"} spire:266584
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li#NicolaiHelling98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"}> Hermann Nicolai
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+C.+Helling"} Robert C. Helling
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supermembranes and M(atrix) Theory
                  %em Trieste 1998, Nonperturbative aspects of strings, branes and supersymmetry
                  (1998) 29-74 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9809103"}> arXiv:hep-th/9809103
                  ,
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/476366"} spire:476366
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em Membranes and Matrix Models
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0206192"}> arXiv:hep-th/0206192
                  ]
              %li#DasguptaNicolaiPlefka02
                %p
                  Arundhati Dasgupta,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Plefka"} Jan Plefka
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em An Introduction to the Quantum Supermembrane
                  %strong 8
                  1 (2002) and Rev. Mex. Fis. 49S1 (2003) 1-10 [
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201182"}> arXiv:hep-th/0201182
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/582067"} spire:582067
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+van+den+Oord"}> Gijs van den Oord
                  ,
                  %em On Matrix Regularisation of Supermembranes
                  MSc thesis (2006) (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/vdOoord-Supermembranes.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meer+Ashwinkumar"}> Meer Ashwinkumar
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lennart+Schmidt"} Lennart Schmidt
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meng-Chwan+Tan"} Meng-Chwan Tan
                  %em
                    Matrix Regularization of Classical Nambu Brackets and Super
                    = succeed "-Branes" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.06666"}> arXiv:2103.06666
                  )
            %p
              The generalization to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pp-wave+spacetimes"} pp-wave spacetimes
              (leading to the
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            %ul
              %li#DSJVR02
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keshav+Dasgupta"}> Keshav Dasgupta
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mohammad+Sheikh-Jabbari"} Mohammad Sheikh-Jabbari
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"} Mark Van Raamsdonk
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Matrix Perturbation Theory For M-theory On a PP-Wave
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205185"} arXiv:hep-th/0205185
              %li#DSJVR02
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keshav+Dasgupta"}> Keshav Dasgupta
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mohammad+Sheikh-Jabbari"} Mohammad Sheikh-Jabbari
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"} Mark Van Raamsdonk
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Matrix Perturbation Theory For M-theory On a PP-Wave
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205185"} arXiv:hep-th/0205185
            %p See also
            %ul
              %li#DuffInamiPopeSezginStelle88
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
                  , T. Inami,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Pope"} Christopher Pope
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Semiclassical Quantization of the Supermembrane
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/247064"} spire:247064
              %li#KabatTaylor97
                %p
                  Daniel Kabat,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Washington+Taylor"} Washington Taylor
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Spherical membranes in Matrix theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711078"} arXiv:hep-th/9711078
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
                  ,
                  %em Towards Covariant Quantization of the Supermembrane
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201151"}> arXiv:hep-th/0201151
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  Qiang Jia,
                  %em On matrix description of D-branes
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.00142"}> arXiv:1907.00142
                  )
            %p
              A new kind of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+series"} perturbation series
              for the quantized super-membrane:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olaf+Lechtenfeld"}> Olaf Lechtenfeld
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                %em A perturbative expansion scheme for supermembrane and matrix theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.00346"}> arXiv:2109.00346
                )
            %p
              Relation to the string
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton"} dilaton
              under
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fundamental Membranes and the String Dilaton
                %strong 2022
                219 (2022) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP09(2022)219"}> doi:10.1007/JHEP09(2022)219
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.05822"} arXiv:2208.05822
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                So Katagiri:
                %em A Lorentz Covariant Matrix Model for Bosonic M2-Branes: Nambu Brackets and Restricted Volume-Preserving Deformations
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.05940"}> arXiv2504.05940
                ]
